\title{HybriFlow: Processing, Quality Control and Follow-Up Analysis of HybriSpot HPV Genotyping Results}
\description{
Turns the raw per-sample Excel probe files and PDF reports produced by the HybriSpot HPV genotyping platform into a single, quality-controlled sample database. The package links each Excel file to its PDF report, calls genotype results, evaluates hybridisation, amplification and no-template controls, flags discordant probe positions and repeated samples, extracts reagent lot numbers and dates from the PDF reports, and checks that the Excel-derived and PDF-reported HPV status agree. For longitudinal studies it classifies each participant by what happened to her baseline genotypes (persisted, cleared, newly acquired, or a combination of these) and produces genotype-level persistence, clearance and acquisition figures, an Excel workbook and an HTML report. HybriFlow is an independent tool and is not developed, endorsed or supported by the manufacturer of the HybriSpot platform.
